<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the binaries bundled in Contents/Resources/bin. NOT for Carabiner.app
  itself, whose entitlements XcodeGen generates from project.yml.

  yt-dlp and gallery-dl are PyInstaller one-file builds: at startup they unpack their own
  Python framework and shared objects into a temp directory and dlopen them. Those
  libraries carry the signature they were built with, not ours. Once the launcher is
  re-signed with Hardened Runtime it becomes a hardened process, and library validation
  refuses to map a library whose Team ID differs from the process's, so the tool dies
  immediately with "mapping process and mapped file (non-platform) have different Team
  IDs".

  This has to be on the *binaries*, not on the app. They run as child processes, and a
  process is governed by its own signature; nothing is inherited from the parent. Putting
  it only on Carabiner.app (the obvious reading) leaves both tools broken.

  This is a real weakening of the hardening, and it is load-bearing. The alternative is
  one-folder PyInstaller builds with every nested shared object signed by us; revisit if
  that ever becomes cheaper than this.

  Careful when editing this comment: a double hyphen is illegal inside an XML comment, and
  codesign fails with "AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error" rather than anything about XML.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
